"""Single-point mutants of src/core/factorized_rbf.py for tools/mutants.py (the WP1 study's engine), run against tests/test_factorized_rbf.py:
the 77 mutants of round 156's referee re-anchored on the current source (M01-M67, N01-N07, X01-X04; N03-N07 re-anchored after the
solver-fallback bookkeeping of round 156), the fallback bookkeeping (N05b, N08-N11) and the branch-pair code (P: PaperPairs, F: form_ratio,
T: formed_threshold, S: atom_summary) -- 123 mutants -- and, added in the PZ2 round, the referee's Q04 (PowerN.init) and V01-V05 (the
form_times and earliness that `atom_summary` gained for part K's coupled targets).

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp ../src/core/factorized_rbf --tests tests/test_factorized_rbf.py \\
        --raw results/chaos/parametrization_raw.npz --md results/chaos/parametrization.md --out-env PZ_OUT \\
        --spec tools/mutants/wp1_factorized_own.py --work <scratch dir> [--only ID,ID] [-k EXPR]

(--exp names the mutated file relative to experiments/; the tool's md column and fr_rc are meaningless for these mutants: --from-raw does
not import the mutated module as a script.) An (id, what, old, new, k) tuple replaces the k-th occurrence (from 0) of `old` in the file.

Result of the first 123 against tests/test_factorized_rbf.py ALONE (that is the tool's kill criterion: pytest -x on the tests file; not
"the tests and the experiment's checks"): 122 killed by an assertion failure ("1 failed" in pytest's last line in every kill, no timeout, no
collection error; the PZ2 referee re-ran all 123 in 1,488 s and the unmutated control passes) and 1 equivalent, S14: the guard `if np.any(np.isnan(mt))` of
`atom_summary` duplicates the propagation of a NaN through np.max (the same expression in `analyse` has no guard of its own; 0 differences on
400 random records with NaN times: the PZ2 referee's check). Two of the 122 are soft kills: P12 (PaperPairs started with amp0 = a0) is equivalent in behaviour,
since `PaperPairs.init` never reads `amp0`, and is killed by an attribute assertion (`ro.amp0 == 0.0`); N01 (the default LSODA budget
disabled) is killed by a constant pin (`FR.STIFF_BUDGET == 150000`), not by a stall. 21 functions and methods had no mutant at all (PowerN,
_unpack, Unit, pts, Linear.init among them); of the PZ2 referee's 10 mutants in them 6 were killed and 4 survived: Q04 (PowerN.init with
s = eps: no engine test pinned the start of D4 and D5, the conserved-quantity test is blind to it) was the substantive one and is now killed by
`test_power_readouts_start_at_s_equal_sqrt_eps_like_cubic3`; Q05 (assert N >= 1), Q09 (Linear.init's random sign, unused) and Q10 (equivalent)
remain, unadded.

PZ2 round, against tests/test_factorized_rbf.py (now 69 tests; the unmutated control passes): Q04 is killed by the new
`test_power_readouts_start_at_s_equal_sqrt_eps_like_cubic3` (pytest: "1 failed, 66 passed"), V01-V05 by the new
`test_atom_summary_earliness_is_one_minus_formation_over_entry_in_the_paths_entry_order` ("1 failed, 67 passed" each). The referee's E01 and E04
are mutants of experiments/exp_parametrization.py, not of the engine, and survived the tests of a00b405; with the new tests/test_parametrization.py
(43 tests; control "43 passed", its md regenerated byte-identically) both are killed (E01 "1 failed, 19 passed", E04 "1 failed, 20 passed"):

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_parametrization --tests tests/test_parametrization.py \\
        --raw results/chaos/parametrization_raw.npz --md results/chaos/parametrization.md --out-env PZ_OUT --workers-env PZ_WORKERS \\
        --extra results/chaos/transit_certificate_raw.npz --extra results/chaos/parametrization.md --spec <spec> --work <scratch dir>

with, in experiments/exp_parametrization.py, E01 = `exact=bool(a['exact'] and b['n_atoms'] == len(As))` -> `exact=bool(a['exact'])` (cell_atoms: K units
matched to K features can sit on K - 1 atoms) and E04 = `thr = FR.formed_threshold(tgt['As'])` -> `thr = 0.009` (job_k: the prediction at the design's
threshold; invisible on the design and within the 0.02 tolerance of the old raw test on the other targets). The --extra files are needed: without
them even the unmutated control fails (the target sample reads the certificate raw, the report test compares the md). Fifteen further mutants of
the PZ2 round's new experiment code (coupled_targets, the rule's helpers, job_kc, job_ka, the scan variant of job_l, the job lists of part_K and
part_L, run_k, job_d, the grid and the separation of job_k) were run the same way: 14 killed, and X04 (`rule_threshold` with log10 in place of ln)
survives as an equivalent mutant, since a ratio of two logarithms does not depend on the base."""

